# bmcd is a cargo package: Buildroot fetches the GitHub archive, runs
# `cargo vendor`, and stores the re-packed archive (the "-cargo2" suffix)
# -- so the sum covers the vendored crates too, exactly as Buildroot does
# for its own cargo packages.
#
# THE SUM DEPENDS ON THE RUST TOOLCHAIN, not just on the commit. The
# archive is named after the commit alone, so a stale one in dl/ looks
# right and hashes wrong. Measured on 2026-09-08 against commit 9b5cffa:
# rust-bin 1.85.0 vendored
# 9815f9cb190773112439b8979222f45ee79124f15ace2d29c5484141be679f65,
# rust-bin 1.98.1 vendored
# 84b9825371b085cea0f21ef03efd50893cfb16c0806cecb98c3700d605b44b9c.
# Recompute after any Rust bump, from a tree re-extracted AFTER the bump --
# buildroot_patches/ are applied at extract time, so a tree extracted
# before the patch changed still carries the old toolchain and produces the
# old sum under a name that looks correct.
#
# Computed with buildroot/local.mk REMOVED. A dev override rsyncs a working
# tree instead of downloading the pinned archive, so a hash computed with one
# in place would describe whatever happened to be on the workstation.
#
# The version is commit 0df4e5b on excavador-turing/bmcd branch `hive`,
# released as v2.30.0: a proxy holding a client certificate from a configured
# CA can name the human it authenticated. That is what lets the fleet
# interface reach a board without holding root's password for it, and it is
# off unless `tls.client_ca` is set -- which a board does not ship with, so
# this release changes nothing on a board nobody has configured.
#
# The listener does change: client certificates are now REQUESTED (PEER
# without FAIL_IF_NO_PEER_CERT) when a CA is configured. A client that offers
# none still gets through to the login page, which is the break-glass path.
#
# Measured 2026-09-11 with the pinned container, from a tree with no
# buildroot/local.mk: `make bmcd-source` against a zeroed expectation reported
# got d9f704f7, then re-run to confirm it fetches and verifies cleanly --
# "OK (sha256: d9f704f7...)".
#
# Worth knowing: the sum is of the archive NAME as well as its contents. The
# same commit pinned short (0df4e5b93a53) hashes to 6a0d3d71 and pinned in
# full to d9f704f7, because the version string is the archive's name and its
# top-level directory. Compute it for the exact string that will ship.
sha256  d9f704f710226af7aff4d7322ca577dc12ff5326209f55aaa2aa486909d5b1f1  bmcd-0df4e5b93a534a0b30e941fb7675edd4532a8fa8-cargo2.tar.gz
sha256  809fa1ed21450f59827d1e9aec720bbc4b687434fa22283c6cb5dd82a47ab9c0  LICENSE
